# UI copy — plain language

Write for players and organizers, not developers. Short beats thorough.

## Principles

- **One short sentence** for page ledes and section hints. Cut second sentences unless they change what the user should do.
- Prefer everyday words over product/infra jargon.
- Explain chess terms only when the user must act on them (e.g. where to find a FIDE ID).
- Errors tell the user what happened and what to try next — never internals.

## Avoid in user-facing UI

| Don't say | Say instead |
|---|---|
| OAuth, PKCE, callback, webhook | link / sign-in / connect |
| configured on this server / env vars | isn’t available right now |
| ISO (country) | country code (e.g. PH) |
| OTB / modality | OTB / Lichess (chess players know OTB) |
| allow list, cron, cached, API, NDJSON | omit or paraphrase |
| public profile / shareable link | your profile / profile link |
| invalid state, session (tech) | Something went wrong / timed out |
| federation (alone) | country (or show the code with “country”) |
| verified (unexplained) | confirmed |

Legal/privacy pages and organizer deep-dive guides may keep precise terms when accuracy requires it. Flash messages, buttons, filters, badges, and empty states on player pages must stay plain.

## Examples

```svelte
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<p class="page-lede">
  Browse players sorted by cached FIDE standard when linked (refreshed daily by cron).
</p>
<span>OAuth not configured</span>
<label>Country (ISO)</label>

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<p class="page-lede">Find players by name or chess account.</p>
<span>Linking unavailable</span>
<label>Country code</label>
```

```js
// ❌ BAD
'Lichess OAuth is not configured on this server.'
'Country must be a 2-letter ISO code'

// ✅ GOOD
'Lichess linking isn’t available right now. Please try again later.'
'Use a 2-letter country code, like PH or US'
```
